    ]}
  />

  <h2 id="which-to-choose">Which Should You Choose?</h2>
  
  <h3>Choose MP4 if:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>You want the video to play on absolutely any device (older iPhones, Smart TVs, offline players).</li>
    <li>You plan to edit the video in professional software like Premiere Pro or Final Cut.</li>
    <li>You are sharing the file directly with someone else and don't know what device they use.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Choose WebM if:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>You are downloading videos specifically to re-upload to a website.</li>
    <li>You want the smallest possible file size while retaining good quality (especially with VP9 codec).</li>
    <li>You primarily watch videos in a modern web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge).</li>
  </ul>
